__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
config/secrets.yaml
*.db
# Match the whole class, not just `.env` — a stray `.env copy` / `.env.bak` /
# `.env.local` holds the same live credentials and was previously committable.
.env*
!.env.example
docker-compose.override.yml
# Local CodeGraph index — machine-specific, rebuilt on demand.
.codegraph/
# Backtest and research output. A few files under here are nonetheless TRACKED,
# force-added with `git add -f` because they are evidence of record rather than
# regenerable output: the KAN-55 edge evaluation (`output/edge/`) and the two
# stability surfaces it cites (`output/stability/`). A single-use holdout was
# spent to produce them and cannot be spent again, so they are not reproducible
# by re-running. This stays a deny-by-default rule with deliberate exceptions —
# NOT a negation pattern — so a future run does not get committed by accident.
# The 249MB baseline they were computed from is still ignored; the artifacts
# carry its sha256 instead. See docs/operations/incumbent-edge-evaluation.md.
output/
.DS_Store
.worktrees/
data/cache/*.json
.superpowers/
*.private.md

# Retrained model versions accumulate one file per run; the CANONICAL model is
# committed deliberately (models/signal_quality_model.txt, 178KB). It is
# deterministic (seed=42) but only reproducible from a backtest artifact that
# is itself gitignored at 261MB — and the tests that score against a real
# Booster are the ones that caught --ml-filter being broken for every trained
# model. Gitignoring it would make those tests skip in CI and let that defect
# class return unseen.
models/signal_quality_v*.txt
models/signal_quality_v*.meta.json
